\par \sect\sectd\sectunlocked1\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1134\margrsxn1134\margtsxn1134\margbsxn1134\ltrsect\sbknone\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa120\keepn\dbch\af5\dbch\af6\afs28\loch\f4\fs28{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Basic Description}
\par \pard\plain \s17\sl288\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The Excel GETPIVOTDATA function extracts data from an Excel Pivot Table }
\par \pard\plain \s17\sl288\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The format of the function is : }
\par \pard\plain \s17\sl288\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sb0\sa0{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
GETPIVOTDATA( data_field, pivot_table, [field1], [item1], [field2], [item2], ...) }
\par \pard\plain \s17\sl288\slmult1\sb0\sa140\rtlch \ltrch\loch

\par \pard\plain \s17\sl288\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
where the arguments are as follows: }
\par \trowd\trql\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clvertalc\cellx1352\clvertalc\cellx1548\clvertalc\cellx9972\pard\plain \s21\intbl{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
data_field}\cell\pard\plain \s21\intbl{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
-}\cell\pard\plain \s21\intbl{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The pivot table data field (ie. the value(s) in the center of the table) that you want to retrieve }\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clvertalc\cellx1352\clvertalc\cellx1548\clvertalc\cellx9972\pard\plain \s21\intbl{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
pivot_table}\cell\pard\plain \s21\intbl{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
-}\cell\pard\plain \s21\intbl{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A reference to a range of cells within a Pivot Table (used to specify the pivot table to be searched) }\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clvertalc\cellx1352\clvertalc\cellx1548\clvertalc\cellx9972\pard\plain \s21\intbl{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
[field1], [item1],\line [field2], [item2],\line etc}\cell\pard\plain \s21\intbl{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
-}\cell\pard\plain \s21\intbl\sb0\sa150{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Up to 126 optional pairs of fields and item names, (ie. The rows and columns headers and individual categories) for which you want the returned value. }
\par \pard\plain \s21\intbl\sb0\sa150{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Note: The item values should be entered as follows: }
\par \pard\plain \s21\intbl\li150\ri0\lin150\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa150{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
- \~\~ Numbers can be entered directly }
\par \pard\plain \s21\intbl\li150\ri0\lin150\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa150{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
- \~\~ Dates should be entered as date serial numbers or by using the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "http://www.excelfunctions.net/ExcelDateFunction.html" }{\fldrslt {\cf2\ul\ulc0\langfe255\alang255\lang255\rtlch \ltrch\loch
date function}{}}}\rtlch \ltrch\loch
 }
\par \pard\plain \s21\intbl\li150\ri0\lin150\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa150{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
- \~\~ Times should be entered as decimals or by using the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "http://www.excelfunctions.net/Excel-Time-Function.html" }{\fldrslt {\cf2\ul\ulc0\langfe255\alang255\lang255\rtlch \ltrch\loch
time function}{}}}\rtlch \ltrch\loch
 }
\par \pard\plain \s21\intbl\li150\ri0\lin150\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa150{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
- \~\~ Text values should be entered in quotations }\cell\row\pard\pard\plain \s17\sl288\slmult1\sb0\sa140\rtlch \ltrch\loch

\par \pard\plain \s17\sl288\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Note that, if the requested fields are not visible in the specified Pivot Table, the Getpivotdata function returns the #REF! error. }
\par \pard\plain \s17\sl288\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The easiest way to input the Getpivotdata function is simply to type "=" into a cell and then click on the Pivot Table value that you want to return. Excel automatically inserts the Getpivotdata function into the active cell. }
